[75.659793, "o", "QUARTERLY INTEGRITY AUDIT RESOLUTION\r\n=====================================\r\n\r\nStatus: RESOLVED - Clean audit achieved (all files verified, exit code 0)\r\n\r\nProblem Summary:\r\n- check_integrity.py was reporting 13 failures (not 3 as initially thought)\r\n- 10 binary files failed with UTF-8 decoding errors\r\n- 3 text files showed hash mismatches\r\n- Manual sha256sum checks on the same files passed correctly\r\n\r\nRoot Cause:\r\n- The check_integrity.py script was opening files in TEXT mode ('r')\r\n- Text mode attempts to decode file contents as UTF-8, which fails for binary files\r\n- Text mode may also apply platform-specific line-ending conversions\r\n- The standard sha256sum command uses BINARY mode, which is why manual checks worked\r\n\r\nSolution Applied:\r\n- Modified compute_hash() function in check_integrity.py\r\n- Changed: open(filepath, 'r') → open(filepath, 'rb')\r\n- Removed: .encode('utf-8') step (no longer needed for binary data)\r\n- This makes the script behave identically to sha256sum\r\n\r\nVerification Results:\r\n- All "]
[75.659897, "o", "38 files now pass integrity verification\r\n- Script exits with status 0 (success)\r\n- No files were corrupted\r\n- Manifest was correct\r\n- Ops team was correct that nothing was modified\r\n\r\nBackup:\r\n- Original script saved as check_integrity.py.backup\r\n"]
